# Services and data

GraphQL documents live in `apps/<app>/src/lib/queries/<domain>.ts`. Domain logic lives in `apps/<app>/src/lib/services/api/<domain>.ts`. Routes call the service, never `createHygraphClients()` directly. Read `packages/hygraph/.instructions.md` or `packages/mistral/.instructions.md` when the change touches those packages.

## Shape

- Export a strategy factory and a default instance: `createHygraphBookmarkStrategy()` and `bookmarkService`
- The factory calls `createHygraphClients(env)` with `$env/dynamic/private`
- The interface lists every operation (`list`, `getById`, `create`, `update`, `delete`)
- Queries go through `executeQuery` (returns `null` on failure, caller returns an empty list). Mutations go through `executeMutation` and `publishContent`
- Inputs and results are exported types. Results use `{ success, data?, error? }`
- Limits and field bounds come from `CONSTANTS` in that app's `$lib/config/Constants.ts`, not magic numbers
- Shared checks go in `$lib/services/validation/`. Slugs go through `generateSlug`

Add a new Hygraph field to the query and to `$lib/types` together. Re-export the service from `$lib/services/index.ts`.

`@mnb/hygraph`, `@mnb/mistral`, and `apps/tidal/src/lib/tidal/` are server-only. Do not import them from a `.svelte` file. Mistral's `completeJson` takes the API key as an argument.
